From 81b777e1789a1e1496ce6c849cb15bc969841660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:50:05 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Controls: two-button moves on one key, the mouse wheel, key
 prompts

Keyboard players asked for three things: one key for a move the game
makes from two buttons, the mouse wheel in the game's menus, and prompts
that show their keys.

A profile can list moves made from two of the PSP's buttons together
(GameProfile::combos, a ComboControl each: the settings.ini key, the
menu's label, the buttons and a default key). Keyboard and mouse lists a
row for each after the PSP's controls (actions Combo1 to Combo8), and the
key presses all of the move's buttons in the same read. A key that
already belongs to another control moves as with any row; the classic
layout keeps the combos' keys but for those it uses.

Wheel Up and Wheel Down are bindings like a key (kWheelUp, kWheelDown),
captured by turning the wheel. Each notch presses its control for two of
the game's pad reads and lets it go for two (input::WheelPresses), so a
list moves one row per notch however fast the wheel turns; at most four
notches wait, and turning back drops them. <prefix>_WHEEL_HOLD and
<prefix>_WHEEL_GAP change the reads. The wheel counts while the window
has the pointer, as the mouse's buttons do. A settings.ini from before
held every binding, so the wheel bindings of the defaults
(keyboard_defaults) are added to it once, where their control has room
and the wheel is bound nowhere else; settings.ini then carries
input.bindings_version=2. The input script has a wheel step.

Button prompts has a Keyboard style (PromptStyle, PromptSetting,
PadKind). Automatic shows it when player 1 last pressed a bound key or
mouse button rather than their gamepad, or has none (not on a phone
without one, which is played on the screen). ButtonPrompts::keys holds
the first key or mouse button bound to each of the PSP's buttons, so a
profile drawing the game's symbols can show them, and a rebinding draws
them again.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows (clang build, USA disc), keyboard
only: each combo key sent its two buttons in one read and the game made
the move; wheel notches moved the main menu one row each; an older
settings.ini gained the wheel on D-pad up and down; rebinding triangle
and square in the menu redrew the game's prompts with the new keys. The
input tests cover the combos, the wheel's names, presses and migration,
and the keyboard style; they, the settings tests and the profile tests
pass. Not tested: a real wheel or a touchpad's fractional scrolling, the
keyboard as player 2, Linux, Android, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
